WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.410
An alkaline AA cell gives about 1.5 volts.

2
00:00:04.460 --> 00:00:08.630
A lithium coin cell, small
and flat, gives about 3 volts.

3
00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:11.690
A tiny cell, with twice the voltage.

4
00:00:11.740 --> 00:00:14.330
So where does the extra voltage come from?

5
00:00:14.380 --> 00:00:20.370
Why does a lithium coin cell give 3 volts,
when an alkaline AA cell gives only 1.5?

6
00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:25.670
In this mission, you'll calculate a cell
potential from two standard electrode potentials,

7
00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:27.910
and decide whether a
reaction is spontaneous.

8
00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:30.790
You'll link cell
potential to Gibbs energy,

9
00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:34.830
and find the number of electrons
transferred in an equation.

10
00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:39.470
Your mission: explain why a lithium
cell gives such a large voltage.
